If you're installing multiple patches, there's a chance they'll
interfere with each other, since the way it works is basically:
"Look for code that looks like 'foo' near line 42", then put 'bar'
after it.  It'll still work if it's a bit different, but if another
patch has changed a lot of nearby lines, it might fail and you'll need
to make the modifications manually.  In general, try installing small
patches first, then large patches, since less will have changed and
the large patch will have a better chance of working.  But if it still
doesn't work, you might want to then reverse the order, since it's
quicker to install a small patch by hand than a large one.


